{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422729-learning-mentors-libraries-etc","id":1422729,"title":"Learning, Mentors, Libraries etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-09T05:18:02-08:00","id":1422729,"title":"Learning, Mentors, Libraries etc.","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I'm looking for some ideas how to handle learning new things or improving during downtime.<br /> How do you decide how much time it takes to find a teacher, if the PC doesn't have the Mentor background? <br /> Can such a teacher power learning time as a Mentor would? If so, what advantages does a Mentor give then?<br /> How long does it take to learn a new Sphere or increase it? What's about Abilities and Attributes?<br /> <br /> Thank you for reading!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T12:17:25-08:00","id":1422800,"title":"","content":"Finding a teacher question is a bit too variable to answer for a PC without a Mentor background. You'd want to figure out how rare the teacher who can teach that subject at the desired level is.Destiny or Status or other Backgrounds that aid in navigating Mage society should help find the teacher.<br /> <br /> For sphere learning time, the Bitter Road had a chart on page 73. The chart is set for a Library or a Mentor, so if the teacher doesn't count as either a Library provider or a Mentor, the time would be the default time per RAW. Mentors speed up learning time and help PCs. If using the sphere learning chart, then the difficulty would be [sphere level learning+3] rolled against the Mentor rating. Successes after the first would reduce the time by that factor--thus 2 successes would halve the time and three would make it one-third.<br /> <br /> There's not a similar chart that I am aware of for Abilities and Attributes. However, keep in mind that when you start getting into 3-dot Abilities you are in the professional range and few people are that good. 4 dots and 5 dots should be very uncommon. The closer a PC was to those levels, the more plausible it is for them to pick up the next dots. Someone with nothing in an Ability should not get up to professional level in a month. A PC at three dots who's experienced and whose concept makes that Ability important might just get 4 dots shortly into play as you reflect new learn.g For attributes, the 4-dot and 5-dot range are quite unusual. Thus, the time to increase an Ability or Attribute is up to you.<br /> <br /> I use GURPS and its learning times to benchmark my Abilities and Attributes learning. Basically, keep doing something and you'll learn a little about it each day. Put in enough time and the XP in Mage, and you get better.<br /> <br /> Or, check out Ars Magica, which has very detailed rules for downtime research.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T16:44:35-08:00","id":1422845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422729-learning-mentors-libraries-etc?p=1422800#post1422800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sphere learning time, the Bitter Road had a chart on page 73.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is helpful, thanks. I think I will adapt it a bit.<br /> <br /> 1, 1 month<br /> 2, 6<br /> 3,12<br /> 4, 60<br /> 5, 120<br /> <br /> To learn the first dot in seven different Spheres would take 7 months, giving the student Perception in every Sphere (counting the minimum 2 he starts with). To raise a single Sphere from 3 to 4 takes over eight times that amount. So, let's (me) even that out a bit. Zero to Five is 199 months. I would think that starting a new Sphere would be almost as challenging as raising a known Sphere from 3 to 4. Increasing difficulty on d10s further advantages the Mage trying to get all the Spheres at 1.<br /> <br /> Averaging 40 months (3 years, four months).<br /> <br /> 1, 4<br /> 2, 20<br /> 3, 40 months<br /> 4, 60 <br /> 5, 76 <br /> <br /> Difficulty Modifier: Whenever a Sphere effect has significant impact on the setting AND changes the caster's Resonance, storyteller records successes scored. All 1s, including on successful rolls, are added to a Quiet Bank. Divide the success total by 10 or more to get a number of Aptitude Points. Actual experience using the Sphere where there is resistance (Earth Consensus or realm with no bonus to that Sphere's use) accumulates a bank of Aptitude Points that can be spent to reduce Library/Mentor roll. Perception Effects do little to change the world, while risky higher level effects are more rewarding. When the player spends Aptitude Points, they pick up that number of temporary Quiet until the Quiet Bank is depleted.<br /> <br /> I think this makes the game more balanced and advancement time more realistic. The carefree Orphan actually gets something for his hard learned lessons in bending the Consensus. The well connected Hermetic can take his time, probably raising Life to ensure he has the longevity needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422729-learning-mentors-libraries-etc?p=1422800#post1422800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not a similar chart that I am aware of for Abilities and Attributes. However, keep in mind that when you start getting into 3-dot Abilities you are in the professional range and few people are that good. 4 dots and 5 dots should be very uncommon. The closer a PC was to those levels, the more plausible it is for them to pick up the next dots. Someone with nothing in an Ability should not get up to professional level in a month. A PC at three dots who's experienced and whose concept makes that Ability important might just get 4 dots shortly into play as you reflect new learn.g For attributes, the 4-dot and 5-dot range are quite unusual. Thus, the time to increase an Ability or Attribute is up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I use a modified version of the old Library Refund system. All refunded XP must be spent on things other than Arete and Spheres. It makes for more balanced characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422729-learning-mentors-libraries-etc?p=1422800#post1422800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use GURPS and its learning times to benchmark my Abilities and Attributes learning. Basically, keep doing something and you'll learn a little about it each day. Put in enough time and the XP in Mage, and you get better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Must check this out soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":".  Math 11-17-2020, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T17:20:44-08:00","id":1422849,"title":"","content":"The base GURPS assumption is that 200 hours of directed study are worth 1 character point. That's enough to buy a mental skill at the lowest level or learn a simple combat move. The GURPS Basic Set covers this, though <i>GURPS Social Engineering: Back to School</i> goes into far more detail than the Basic Set if you want it.<br /> <br /> It's less important in Mage to have one specific system for how characters learn than figuring out one that works for your group. Since being a Master mage is supposed to take decades and being an Adept isn't that quick, either, your times to learn those levels are best reflected as much longer than the lower sphere levels. If you use the Library rule from<i> Bitter Road</i>, there's definitely a reason to get good libraries and mentors. Shaving off time to study is a big deal. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T20:42:24-08:00","id":1422868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422729-learning-mentors-libraries-etc?p=1422849#post1422849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The base GURPS assumption is that 200 hours of directed study are worth 1 character point. That's enough to buy a mental skill at the lowest level or learn a simple combat move.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Jocko Willink, a famous Navy Seal, American police get four hours of combat training per year. Comment at 3:12.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FkytSGayFLk&amp;ab_channel=JoeRoganHighlights\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FkytSGayFLk&amp;ab_channel=JoeRoganHighlights\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FkytSGayFLk&amp;ab_channel=JoeRoganHighlights\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FkytSGayFLk&amp;ab_channel=JoeRoganHighlights </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1422729-learning-mentors-libraries-etc?p=1422849#post1422849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's less important in Mage to have one specific system for how characters learn than figuring out one that works for your group. Since being a Master mage is supposed to take decades and being an Adept isn't that quick, either, your times to learn those levels are best reflected as much longer than the lower sphere levels. If you use the Library rule from<i> Bitter Road</i>, there's definitely a reason to get good libraries and mentors. Shaving off time to study is a big deal. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a system that favors spreading out over mastery actually makes the game more challenging. If I'm a player, I'm going to put twelve freebies into Arete, shop for flaws, child obviously, and have about 13 points to put into Backgrounds. Avatar? 2. If I'm mostly using lower level Spheres, there's not as big a need to reduce difficulties that much. Five points into Library and, &quot;digital please&quot;. Sanctum 5. Resources 1. <br /> <br /> Correspondence 3 to avoid conflict. Make sure I take Life 3. Great. Aging is no problem. Cautiously network with players or friendly NPCs to combine Libraries with. Work on improving the Sanctum. Do Magickal experiments at decreased difficulty. Heal other players at a distance. Spread XP over most of the other Spheres, starting with Mind1 and Prime1. Add Forces to eventually become a Brain-Mage (Mind1, Life3, Forces 2). Directly interface with the digital library to eliminate time spent typing and clicking. This is a passive, insular play-style where everyone starts to be very similar. <br /> <br /> Just because a character has a Sphere at rank 4 doesn't mean they can just blast everything. Higher level Spheres means more severe Paradox when it happens. One of my players, given the option of taking Time 5, has decided not to because of the risks it poses where Paradox is concerned. Higher level Spheres allow each individual player to do things that none of the others can, making their character's knowledge special in some way. Vast amounts of downtime as a requirement discourages interest in Magick that would better define and distinguish the character. <br /> <br /> Other exploits: The Instruction Secondary Skill, BoS p19. Have everyone take this at three with four in Manipulation for double-tens. Everyone's character becomes the same.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T14:44:18-08:00","id":1422963,"title":"","content":"How would you handle the search for a one-time mentor (I call this teacher), e.g. when a character has no library and no mentor, but wishes a teacher for a new Sphere? Would that teacher reduce learning time like mentor? Or less so? Or not at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-10T17:04:40-08:00","id":1422991,"title":"","content":"I'd give the mechanical reductions. Finding a teacher and getting them to teach a character should be a quest, something which takes many adventures or one significant adventure if other resources are used to find the mentor. It's a bit easier to answer the question if you have an example to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T01:44:40-08:00","id":1423029,"title":"","content":"An Example:<br /> The Chorister Character of my group wants to learn Forces 1. He doesn't have the Mentor or Library background. He's located at New Orleans where he's been living for about 8 months now. <br /> Another character has the Mentor background with 5 points, and that player (a minmax player) surely would argue that it would be unfair to give any advantages to the Chorister, because he doesn't have the appropriate background. It should be fair for both. <br /> Is that enough information or do you need more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T05:00:31-08:00","id":1423038,"title":"","content":"Backgrounds typically are earned and raised trough play and the narrative. Getting a &quot;teacher&quot;, with mechanical benefits, should be represented by giving points on the Mentor background.<br /> <br /> This doesn't need to cost xp. Traditionally it's given free - you paid for it by interpretating the whole process as part of the narrartive (and minmax getting angry would be a bonus because WoD hates them). If you don't like narrative rewards, some books make the player pay 2xp per Backround dot before reaping the benefits.<br /> <br /> All that being said, a 5 dots Mentor it's a really powerful character, a coveted teacher even from the perspective of relatively powerful mages. Getting someone like that to teach you personally should be quite a feat on part of the player - I think not having to achieve *that* trough playing it's the big advatage of buying it at char gen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-11T11:39:15-08:00","id":1423086,"title":"","content":"For Forces 1, that's something easy to learn compared to a lot of other spheres.The Chorister wanting to learn Forces 1 will, assuming you are using the Bitter Road chart, need about a month to learn with some help from a teacher. This isn't a month of all-day study, but it is a month of regular learning and practice.<br /> <br /> So, if the potential teacher is going to teach the character, they need a compatible magical style--perhaps Paradigm and certainly Practice and Instruments (because there may not be the big shared belief but you've got to have a way to make it work). Alternatively, the character can learn some new Instruments pretty easily.<br /> <br /> The trainer will want some favors or other service for their time and expertise. If a member of the Celestial Chorus, it would likely be less costly than for a member of a faction that doesn't like the Celestial Chorus. This would be some worthwhile favors--helping Sleepers or gathering information or even trading some other information. The Celestial Chorus character could provide these favors directly or find others to do them--NPCs would likely want something to help the character unless they are friends. PCs can help as they wish.<br /> <br /> Tass is a good form of payment as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}